%S A398093 1,1,2,2,4,10,14,20,56,138,306,642,1538,4728,12202,26886,69544,245400,
%T A398093 701914,1703130,5090288,18660732,57617690,153801960,495507676,
%U A398093 1180025386
%N A398093 a(n) is the number of distinct ordered difference sequences of graceful permutations of length n.
%C A398093 For a permutation p = (p_1, ..., p_n) of {1, ..., n}, let d(p) = (|p_2 - p_1|, ..., |p_n - p_{n - 1}|). The permutation p is graceful if d(p) is a permutation of {1, ..., n - 1}. This sequence counts the distinct sequences d(p) arising from graceful permutations.
%H A398093 Michal Adamaszek, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0608513">Efficient enumeration of graceful permutations</a>, arXiv:math/0608513 [math.CO], 2006.
%H A398093 Felix Huber, <a href="/A398093/a398093.txt">Maple program</a>
%F A398093 a(n) = Sum_{k >= 1} A398094(n, k).
%F A398093 a(n) = A006967(n)/2 - Sum_{k >= 2} (k - 1)*A398094(n, k).
%e A398093 a(5) = 4. The only realizable ordered difference sequences are:
%e A398093   (1, 2, 3, 4), arising from (3, 2, 4, 1, 5) and (3, 4, 2, 5, 1);
%e A398093   (1, 2, 4, 3), arising from (2, 3, 5, 1, 4) and (4, 3, 1, 5, 2);
%e A398093   (3, 4, 2, 1), arising from (2, 5, 1, 3, 4) and (4, 1, 5, 3, 2);
%e A398093   (4, 3, 2, 1), arising from (1, 5, 2, 4, 3) and (5, 1, 4, 2, 3).
%p A398093 # See Huber link.
